st demand  for reprocessing into new products while  there are few markets if any in this  region for all the others and jeremy's  final piece of advice is to know before  you throw we have terms for that it's  called wish cycling or aspirational  recycling you know you may be standing  over your bin and holding something in  your hand and you feel that it should be  recyclable but you're not quite sure  don't just throw something in the bin  thinking hey you know what they'll  figure it out at the recycling center  that actually can do more harm than good  so when in doubt find out or simply when  in doubt throw it out  well i asked jeremy to grade southern  nevadans now on how well we're doing it  recycling on a scale of one to five  because we've been at this for a while  right  and he gave us a three  and he said there's always room for  improvement  so  you know recycling was going up we were  improving improving and then the  pandemic  and the numbers kind of came down  and so we need to go back up so we're  we're passing we're passing  we're not really in that a b category  we're getting a c and i think it's like  he said you know you just got to know  what's acceptable and how to throw it in  the big blue cart keep it all loose  don't bag your recyclables and look for  the arrows on the plastic bottles and  containers and tubs one two and five  said they take one two and five but if  you have a four does that mean you  should just throw it out yeah or find  another use for it a lot of times you  can take those containers and reuse them  for something  put a plant in them you know or use them  for potting or you know put them in your  pantry and put other stuff in them or  okay to put them in your laundry room  and use them but you know i reuse reuse  recycle um it's it's just however your  mindset is  to
 

